<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>SADL IDP · How the numbers did</title>
<style>
{% include "_style.j2" %}
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
th { overflow-wrap: normal; word-break: normal; }
td:first-child, th:first-child { white-space: nowrap; }
.glossary { padding-left: 4px; } .glossary li { margin: 6px 0; }
.scroll table { min-width: 520px; }
.scroll td:first-child, .scroll th:first-child { position: sticky; left: 0; background: var(--card); }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.views > label { margin: 0 6px 8px 0; }
.views > label.wk { padding: 4px 11px; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 500; }
{% for v in (s.views if s else []) %}#view-{{ v.key }}:checked + label { background: var(--accent); color: var(--card); border-color: var(--accent); }
#view-{{ v.key }}:checked ~ #vpanel-{{ v.key }} { display: block; }
{% endfor %}.headline { font-size: 1rem; margin: 4px 0 0; }
.calls li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2em 1fr; gap: 4px; padding: 5px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: .9rem; }
.calls li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
.calls li.hit .mark { color: var(--start); font-weight: 700; } .calls li.miss .mark { color: var(--bad); font-weight: 700; }
.calls li.ref { color: var(--ref); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
{%- macro f1(x) -%}{% if x is none %}—{% else %}{{ '%.1f'|format(x) }}{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro pct(x) -%}{% if x is none %}—{% else %}{{ (x * 100)|round|int }}%{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro runs(b) -%}{% if b is none %}—{% elif b|abs < 0.5 %}about right{% elif b > 0 %}{{ '%.1f'|format(b) }} pts high{% else %}{{ '%.1f'|format(-b) }} pts low{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro ranks(r, n) -%}{% if r is none %}not enough games yet{% elif r < 0.1 %}barely ({{ '%.2f'|format(r) }}){% elif r < 0.3 %}weakly ({{ '%.2f'|format(r) }}){% elif r < 0.5 %}moderately ({{ '%.2f'|format(r) }}){% else %}well ({{ '%.2f'|format(r) }}){% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro view(v, dbr) -%}
  {% set ss = v.by_slot %}{% set single = v.weeks|length == 1 %}
  {% set live = v.suggestions.live %}{% set reb = v.suggestions.rebuilt %}
  <p class="headline">{% if single %}Week {{ v.weeks[0] }}{% else %}Weeks {{ v.weeks[0] }}–{{ v.weeks[-1] }}{% endif %}:
    {% if live.decided or reb.decided %}suggestions paid off {{ live.hits + reb.hits }} of {{ live.decided + reb.decided }}{% if reb.decided and not live.decided %} (rebuilt){% endif %}{% else %}no suggestions decided{% endif %};
    projections missed by {{ f1(ss.DL.mae) }} (DL), {{ f1(ss.LB.mae) }} (LB) and {{ f1(ss.DB.mae) }} (DB) points on average.
    {% if v.provisional %}<small>Provisional: stat corrections still possible.</small>{% endif %}</p>
  <section aria-labelledby="close-h-{{ v.key }}">
    <h2 id="close-h-{{ v.key }}">How close were the projections?</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p>For the {{ s.n_eval }} best-projected players at each position{{ '' if single else ' each week' }}, our number missed by
        {{ f1(ss.DL.mae) }} (DL), {{ f1(ss.LB.mae) }} (LB) and {{ f1(ss.DB.mae) }} (DB) points on average.
        {% if not single %}{% set part = s.weekly|selectattr('week', 'in', v.weeks)|selectattr('partial_slots')|map(attribute='week')|list %}{% if part %}Week{{ 's' if part|length > 1 else '' }} {{ part|join(', ') }} {{ 'are' if part|length > 1 else 'is' }} only partly covered (the projections saved before kickoff cover some games only), so {{ 'they are' if part|length > 1 else 'it is' }} left out of these numbers.{% endif %}{% endif %}
        {% if ss.DL.mae_base %}A simple guess, each player's own average so far, missed by {{ f1(ss.DL.mae_base) }} / {{ f1(ss.LB.mae_base) }} / {{ f1(ss.DB.mae_base) }} on the same players (ours: {{ f1(ss.DL.mae_ours_on_base) }} / {{ f1(ss.LB.mae_ours_on_base) }} / {{ f1(ss.DB.mae_ours_on_base) }}).{% endif %}</p>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Pos</th><th class="num">Avg miss (pts)</th><th>Runs high/low</th><th>{{ 'Top-12 hits' if single else 'Ranks players right' }}</th></tr>
        {% for slot in slots %}{% set x = ss[slot] %}
        <tr><td>{{ slot }}{% if x.partial %} <small>partial</small>{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ f1(x.mae) }}</td><td>{{ runs(x.bias) }}</td><td>{% if single %}{{ top12(x.top12) }}{% else %}{{ ranks(x.spearman, x.n) }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table>
      {% if single %}<p class="note">Top-12 hits: of our 12 best-projected, how many finished in the actual top 12 (random picks from the 50 would land about 3). How well the order matches is shown season-long only, once there are enough games.</p>{% endif %}
      {% for slot in slots %}{% set b = ss[slot].bias %}{% if b is not none and b|abs >= 1 %}
      <p class="note">{{ slot }} numbers run about {{ '%.1f'|format(b|abs) }} pts {{ 'high' if b > 0 else 'low' }} on average. Suggestions only compare {{ slot }}s with other {{ slot }}s, so a shift shared by all of them changes no suggestion; it isn't corrected.</p>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {% if dbr is not none and dbr < 0.1 %}<p class="note dbnote"><b>DBs:</b> so far this season, the order of the DB projections barely matches the order of the scores (r {{ '%.2f'|format(dbr) }}; last season's waiver DBs: 0.01). Treat DB tiers as rough. A DB's snap share and form, both in his breakdown on the main page, say more than a point or two of projection.</p>{% endif %}
      <details><summary>More stats</summary>
        <div class="scroll"><table>
          <tr><th>Pos</th><th class="num">Player-games</th><th class="num">Typical miss (RMSE)</th><th class="num">Inside ±1 range (aim 68%)</th><th class="num">Inside ±2 (aim 95%)</th><th class="num">Top-12 hits</th><th class="num">R²</th><th class="num">Correlation</th></tr>
          {% for slot in slots %}{% set x = ss[slot] %}
          <tr><td>{{ slot }}</td><td class="num">{{ x.n }}</td><td class="num">{{ f1(x.rmse) }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(x.within1) }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(x.within2) }}</td>
            <td class="num">{{ top12(x.top12) }}</td><td class="num">{{ '%.2f'|format(x.r2) if x.r2 is not none else '—' }}</td><td class="num">{{ '%.2f'|format(x.pearson) if x.pearson is not none else '—' }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </table></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% set srcs = v.by_source or {} %}
  {% if srcs|length > 1 %}
  <section aria-labelledby="src-h-{{ v.key }}">
    <h2 id="src-h-{{ v.key }}">Each source on the same players</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p>The players are picked by all sources together, so no source chooses its own. Each source is scored on the ones it projected; "Covered" is how many of them that was.{% set mid = [] %}{% for w in s.weekly if w.week in v.weeks %}{% for name in w.joined_midweek or [] %}{% set _ = mid.append(s.source_labels.get(name, name) ~ ' in week ' ~ w.week) %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}{% if mid %} A source first read live partway through a week only covers the games still to come ({{ mid|join(', ') }}); projections for games already played are never kept.{% endif %}</p>
      <div class="scroll"><table>
        <tr><th>Source</th><th>Pos</th><th class="num">Avg miss (pts)</th><th>Runs high/low</th><th class="num">Covered</th></tr>
        {% for slot in slots %}
        {% for name, by_slot in srcs.items() %}{% set x = by_slot.get(slot) %}{% if x %}
        <tr><td>{{ s.source_labels.get(name, name) }}</td><td>{{ slot }}</td><td class="num">{{ f1(x.mae) }}</td><td>{{ runs(x.bias) }}</td>
          <td class="num">{{ pct(x.covered / x.pool) if x.pool else '—' }} <small>({{ x.covered }})</small></td></tr>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}
        <tr><td><b>All together</b></td><td>{{ slot }}</td><td class="num"><b>{{ f1(ss[slot].mae) }}</b></td><td>{{ runs(ss[slot].bias) }}</td><td class="num">100% <small>({{ ss[slot].n }})</small></td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section aria-labelledby="sugg-h-{{ v.key }}">
    <h2 id="sugg-h-{{ v.key }}">Did the suggestions pay off?</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p>{% if live.decided %}Live suggestions: {{ live.hits }} of {{ live.decided }} paid off (the suggested player outscored the one he was compared with).{% elif not reb.decided %}No suggestions were decided {{ 'this week' if single else 'yet' }}.{% endif %}
        {% if reb.decided %}{{ 'This week was rebuilt after the fact' if single else 'On the rebuilt weeks' }}: {{ reb.hits }} of {{ reb.decided }} would have paid off.{% endif %}
        Suggestions shown only for reference aren't counted, and a void one (a player who didn't play) isn't either.</p>
      {% if single and v.suggestions.list %}
      <ul class="calls">
        {% for e in v.suggestions.list %}
        <li class="{{ e.outcome or '' }}{% if e.reference %} ref{% endif %}"><span class="mark">{% if e.outcome == 'hit' %}✓{% elif e.outcome == 'miss' %}✗{% else %}·{% endif %}</span>
          <span>{{ e.badge }} <b>{{ e.name }}</b> <small>{{ e.slot }}</small> {{ f1(e.pts) }}{% if e.over_name %} vs {{ e.over_name }} {{ f1(e.over_pts) }}{% endif %}{% if e.p is not none %} <small>({{ [(e.p * 100)|round|int, 99]|min }}% said)</small>{% endif %}{% if e.reference %} <small>for reference</small>{% endif %}{% if e.outcome == 'void' %} <small>void</small>{% endif %}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="tiers-h-{{ v.key }}">
    <h2 id="tiers-h-{{ v.key }}">Do the tiers mean anything?</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      {% set nums = (v.tiers.DL + v.tiers.LB + v.tiers.DB)|map(attribute='tier')|unique|sort %}
      {% if nums %}
      <p>Average score of the players in each tier as shown when you set waivers (the Tuesday sync; rebuilt weeks: before their first game), with the number of player-games. Higher tiers should score more.</p>
      <p class="note">The ± is the margin of error (about 95%): one game swings a player's score by around 7 points, while the waiver players a position shows are usually projected within 2 to 4 points of each other. Where two tiers' ranges overlap, the games {{ 'this week' if single else 'so far' }} can't tell them apart, even if the tiers are right.</p>
      <div class="scroll"><table>
        <tr><th>Tier</th>{% for slot in slots %}<th class="num">{{ slot }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
        {% for n in nums %}
        <tr><td>Tier {{ n }}</td>{% for slot in slots %}{% set t = v.tiers[slot]|selectattr('tier', 'equalto', n)|first %}<td class="num">{% if t %}{{ f1(t.avg) }}{% if t.margin is not none %} <small>±{{ f1(t.margin) }}</small>{% endif %} <small>({{ t.n }})</small>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table></div>
      {% else %}<p class="note">No tiers were saved from before the waiver run {{ 'this week' if single else 'yet' }}.</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro top12(t) -%}{% if t and t[1] %}{{ t[0] }} of {{ t[1] }}{% else %}—{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
<header>
  <h1>How the numbers did</h1>
  <p class="meta">{{ league_name }} · {{ s.season }} season · <a href="index.html">← back to this week</a></p>
</header>
<main>
{% if not s %}
  <p class="note">No week has final stats yet.</p>
{% else %}
  {% set ss = s.season_by_slot %}
  {% set dbr = ss.DB.spearman %}
  <div class="tabs views">
    {% for v in s.views %}<input type="radio" name="view" id="view-{{ v.key }}"{% if loop.first %} checked{% endif %}><label for="view-{{ v.key }}" class="{{ 'wk' if v.key.startswith('w') else 'main' }}">{{ v.label }}</label>{% endfor %}
    {% for v in s.views %}
    <div class="tabpanel" id="vpanel-{{ v.key }}">{{ view(v, dbr) }}</div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="weeks-h">
    <h2 id="weeks-h">Week by week</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p class="note">Average miss in points. "archive" = projections fetched after the week from the sources' archives; "late" = some captured after kickoff.</p>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Wk</th>{% for slot in slots %}<th class="num">{{ slot }}</th>{% endfor %}<th></th></tr>
        {% for w in s.weekly %}
        <tr><td>{{ w.week }}</td>{% for slot in slots %}{% set x = w.by_slot[slot] %}<td class="num">{{ f1(x.mae) }}{% if x.partial %} <small>partial ({{ x.n }})</small>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
          <td><small>{% if w.provisional %}provisional {% endif %}{% if w.backfill %}archive{% endif %}{% if w.late %} · late{% endif %}</small></td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="odds-h">
    <h2 id="odds-h">Are the START/UPGRADE odds honest?</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p>For every pair of pool players at a position, we checked how often the one we favoured actually scored more.
        Odds score (a coin flip is 0.250; lower is better): {% for slot in slots %}{% set x = ss[slot] %}{{ slot }} {% if x.brier is none %}—{% else %}{{ '%.3f'|format(x.brier) }}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
        {% set o = namespace(better=[], even=[], worse=[]) %}{% for slot in slots %}{% set b = ss[slot].brier %}{% if b is not none %}{% if b < 0.245 %}{% set o.better = o.better + [slot] %}{% elif b > 0.255 %}{% set o.worse = o.worse + [slot] %}{% else %}{% set o.even = o.even + [slot] %}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        {% if o.better %}Better than a coin flip at {{ o.better|join(', ') }}. {% endif %}{% if o.even %}About as good as a coin flip at {{ o.even|join(', ') }}. {% endif %}{% if o.worse %}Worse than a coin flip at {{ o.worse|join(', ') }}: the odds there are overconfident. {% endif %}{% if o.even or o.worse %}Treat a 60–75% badge as a slight lean, not a sure thing.{% endif %}</p>
      <details><summary>When we said X%, how often did it happen?</summary>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Pos</th><th class="num">We said</th><th class="num">Happened</th><th class="num">Pairs</th></tr>
          {% for slot in slots %}{% for c in ss[slot].calibration %}
          <tr><td>{{ slot }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(c.said) }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(c.happened) }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.n }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}{% endfor %}
        </table>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="weights-h">
    <h2 id="weights-h">Who gets how much say</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      {% set hist = s.weights_history or [] %}{% set now = hist[-1] if hist else none %}
      <p>{% if s.sources|length == 1 %}Only {{ s.sources[0].name }} so far: it's 100% of every number.{% else %}Each source's share of a player's number when every source has him{% if now %} this week (week {{ now.week }}){% endif %}: {% if now %}{% for name, sh in now.shares.items() %}{{ name }} {{ pct(sh) }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% else %}{% for x in s.sources %}{{ x.name }} {{ pct(x.share) }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}. Where a source has nothing for a player, the others' shares grow to fill its place. A ranking becomes points by giving rank N the Nth-best projection among the players it ranks.{% endif %}</p>
      <p>{% if now and now.method == 'accuracy' %}The shares follow each source's measured accuracy on weeks {{ now.from_weeks|join(', ') }}{% if now.alpha_hat is not none %}; the best mix of projections and rankings on those weeks was {{ pct(now.alpha_hat) }} projections (capped at 20–80%){% endif %}. Every estimate is pulled toward the starting shares (projections {{ pct(s.prior_split) }}, sources equal within each group) until it has many weeks behind it, so one odd week moves little.{% else %}{% set has_rank = s.sources|selectattr('kind', 'equalto', 'rank')|list %}These are the starting shares: {% if has_rank %}projections {{ pct(s.prior_split) }}, rankings {{ pct(1 - s.prior_split) }}, sources equal within each group{% else %}sources equal{% endif %}.{% if now and now.reason %} ({{ now.reason|capitalize }}.){% endif %} From 3 scored weeks on, each source's share follows its measured accuracy.{% endif %} A week uses results up to two weeks before it, and its shares are fixed at its first sync, so they never change under a page you've already seen.</p>
      {% if hist|length > 1 %}
      <details><summary>Shares week by week</summary>
        <div class="scroll"><table>
          {% set names = hist|map(attribute='shares')|map('list')|sum(start=[])|unique|list %}
          <tr><th>Wk</th>{% for n in names %}<th class="num">{{ n }}</th>{% endfor %}<th>Set by</th></tr>
          {% for h in hist %}
          <tr><td>{{ h.week }}</td>{% for n in names %}<td class="num">{% if n in h.shares %}{{ pct(h.shares[n]) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}<td><small>{% if h.method == 'accuracy' %}accuracy (weeks {{ h.from_weeks|join(', ') }}){% else %}starting shares{% endif %}</small></td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </table></div>
      </details>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {% set dst = s.dst_backtest %}
  {% if dst and dst.positions %}
  <section aria-labelledby="dst-h">
    <h2 id="dst-h">Your team-defense idea: tested, not used</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p>{% if dst.passes %}At least one signal passed on last season; see the table. It isn't used until it also helps this season.{% else %}Neither signal helped on last season ({{ dst.season }}, weeks {{ dst.weeks[0] }}–{{ dst.weeks[-1] }}), so neither is used.{% endif %}
        For each position's 60 best-projected players every week, we checked whether a player beat his projection more often when his defense was ranked better by FantasyPros, or when Vegas expected the other team to score less.</p>
      <div class="scroll"><table>
        <tr><th>Pos</th><th>Team D/ST rank</th><th>Opponent's expected points</th><th class="num">Avg miss without → with</th></tr>
        {% for slot in slots %}{% set p = dst.positions.get(slot) %}{% if p %}
        <tr><td>{{ slot }}</td>
          {% for key in ('rank', 'opp_implied') %}{% set x = p.signals[key] %}<td>{{ '%+.2f'|format(x.per_unit) }} per {{ 'place' if key == 'rank' else 'point' }} <small>({{ 'clear' if x.t|abs >= 2 else 'within noise' }}{% if not x.halves_agree %}; flips between halves{% endif %})</small></td>{% endfor %}
          <td class="num">{{ '%.2f'|format(p.mae.projection) }} → {{ '%.2f'|format(p.mae['with signals']) }}</td></tr>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </table></div>
      <p class="note">Points per place of rank (a positive number means a worse-ranked defense's players beat their projection more) and per point of the opponent's expected score. "Within noise" means less than two standard errors from zero. "Avg miss" is on weeks the fit didn't see. It's re-checked with this season's games at weeks 9 and 13.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <details class="slot"><summary><b>What these mean</b></summary>
    <ul class="glossary">
      <li><b>Avg miss</b>: the average gap between our number and what the player scored. Lower is better.</li>
      <li><b>Simple guess</b>: the player's own average so far this season (players with 2+ games). If we don't beat it, the projections add nothing.</li>
      <li><b>Runs high/low</b>: whether our numbers are too high or too low on average.</li>
      <li><b>Ranks players right</b>: how well the order of our numbers matches the order of the scores (0 = no better than random, 1 = perfect). Shown only once there are {{ s.min_corr_n }}+ player-games.</li>
      <li><b>Inside ±1 / ±2 range</b>: how often the score landed within one or two "typical swings" of our number. About 68% and 95% means the ranges are honest.</li>
      <li><b>Typical miss (RMSE)</b>: like the average miss, but big misses count extra.</li>
      <li><b>Top-12 hits</b>: of our 12 best-projected, how many finished in the actual top 12 at the position (ties at 12th count). Picking 12 of the 50 at random would land about 3.</li>
      <li><b>Correlation</b>: how closely our numbers and the scores rise and fall together (0 = not at all, 1 = perfectly).</li>
      <li><b>Odds score</b> (Brier): how good our win probabilities are. A coin flip scores 0.250; lower is better.</li>
      <li><b>R²</b>: below 0 means a flat guess of the average would have done better.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>
{% endif %}
</main>
<footer><p>Computed from the weeks saved in the repo; nothing here changes the numbers on the main page yet. Weeks marked "archive" use projections fetched after the fact from each source's archive.</p></footer>
<script>
(function () {
  var el = location.hash && document.getElementById("view-" + location.hash.slice(1));
  if (el) el.checked = true;
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
